1
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:06,610
Today, I'd like to share JEI's
core repositioning strategy.

2
00:00:07,160 --> 00:00:08,790
Our main message is simple.

3
00:00:09,240 --> 00:00:12,642
JEI must move beyond selling
worksheets and become a company

4
00:00:12,698 --> 00:00:15,760
that designs children's
ability to learn on their own.

5
00:00:17,510 --> 00:00:19,870
Our strategy addresses five questions.

6
00:00:20,420 --> 00:00:21,850
Why do we need to change?

7
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:23,940
What do parents really want?

8
00:00:24,390 --> 00:00:26,100
Where are the opportunities?

9
00:00:26,550 --> 00:00:28,490
How can JEI compete?

10
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:31,750
And how will we deliver
and measure our results?

11
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:33,830
Let's begin with the market.

12
00:00:35,580 --> 00:00:39,640
JEI currently ranks fourth in
Korea's worksheet learning market.

13
00:00:40,090 --> 00:00:44,026
Our three main competitors have
more than 700 locations and

14
00:00:44,093 --> 00:00:48,430
over one million members each,
while JEI has about 300 locations.

15
00:00:48,880 --> 00:00:53,670
Our revenue also fell by
53% between 2010 and 2025.

16
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:56,690
Competing through size alone is difficult.

17
00:00:57,140 --> 00:00:58,960
We need to create a new category.

18
00:01:00,710 --> 00:01:03,340
The number of children
in Korea is declining.

19
00:01:03,790 --> 00:01:10,040
In 2026, about 298,000 children entered
first grade, down 8% from the previous year.

20
00:01:10,490 --> 00:01:16,300
Total private education spending also
fell to 27.5 trillion won in 2025.

21
00:01:16,850 --> 00:01:19,910
However, monthly spending
per elementary student

22
00:01:19,974 --> 00:01:23,480
participating in private
education reached 512,000 won.

23
00:01:23,930 --> 00:01:26,200
Parents are willing to
pay for clear value.

24
00:01:26,750 --> 00:01:31,400
Our focus must shift toward greater value
per customer and stronger retention.

25
00:01:33,150 --> 00:01:36,339
AI-based assessment, personalized
learning, and automatic

26
00:01:36,395 --> 00:01:39,080
grading are becoming common
across the industry.

27
00:01:39,530 --> 00:01:42,670
These features alone are no
longer enough to stand out.

28
00:01:43,220 --> 00:01:47,860
Parents want to save time, reduce their
burden, and see clear learning progress.

29
00:01:48,310 --> 00:01:52,550
JEI must offer something beyond
worksheets and AI features.

30
00:01:54,300 --> 00:01:56,320
Parents have three levels of needs.

31
00:01:56,870 --> 00:02:00,530
Functional needs include suitable
materials and learning reports.

32
00:02:00,980 --> 00:02:05,500
Emotional needs include less worry and
less responsibility for managing study.

33
00:02:05,950 --> 00:02:10,120
But their most important need is for
their children to learn independently.

34
00:02:10,670 --> 00:02:13,424
JEI should focus on developing
this ability through

35
00:02:13,478 --> 00:02:16,070
personalized learning
plans and teacher support.

36
00:02:17,820 --> 00:02:21,020
Parents often stop learning
services for five reasons.

37
00:02:21,570 --> 00:02:23,650
Repetitive learning becomes boring.

38
00:02:24,100 --> 00:02:25,780
Progress is difficult to see.

39
00:02:26,230 --> 00:02:28,190
Parents still manage daily study.

40
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:30,920
Fees increase without clear results.

41
00:02:31,370 --> 00:02:33,780
And AI features make brands look similar.

42
00:02:34,430 --> 00:02:38,420
The main problem is that parents cannot
clearly see their children's growth.

43
00:02:38,870 --> 00:02:41,890
This is the problem JEI must solve.

44
00:02:43,640 --> 00:02:46,580
Our three main competitors
have different strengths.

45
00:02:47,130 --> 00:02:49,610
Daekyo focuses on level-based learning.

46
00:02:50,060 --> 00:02:52,870
Kumon is known for basic
skills and repetition.

47
00:02:53,320 --> 00:02:56,250
Woongjin offers an integrated
learning platform.

48
00:02:56,800 --> 00:03:00,256
But from a customer perspective,
these approaches may leave gaps

49
00:03:00,310 --> 00:03:04,090
in long-term learning direction,
motivation, and personalized support.

50
00:03:04,540 --> 00:03:09,540
JEI should focus on these opportunities
rather than directly copying competitors.

51
00:03:11,290 --> 00:03:14,570
Competitors mainly focus on
how learning is delivered.

52
00:03:15,020 --> 00:03:17,030
But parents want to know something more.

53
00:03:17,580 --> 00:03:20,640
"Where should my child's learning
go over the next three years?"

54
00:03:21,290 --> 00:03:24,630
We believe this creates an
opportunity for Learning Design.

55
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:28,151
JEI can use assessment results
to create personalized

56
00:03:28,209 --> 00:03:30,990
learning paths and help
students stay motivated.

57
00:03:31,440 --> 00:03:33,940
This can become our new
position in the market.

58
00:03:35,690 --> 00:03:39,270
Al Ries explained that positioning
happens in the customer's mind.

59
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:43,350
Customers often rank brands on
a ladder within each category.

60
00:03:43,900 --> 00:03:47,340
JEI is currently number four
in the worksheet market.

61
00:03:47,790 --> 00:03:51,400
Instead of competing on the same
ladder, we can create a new one.

62
00:03:51,950 --> 00:03:54,380
That new category is Learning Design.

63
00:03:54,830 --> 00:03:58,340
Our goal is to become the brand
customers associate with "Design."

64
00:04:00,090 --> 00:04:03,410
We can apply six positioning
principles from Al Ries.

65
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:07,350
First, the Law of the Ladder:
create a new category.

66
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:12,550
Second, the Law of the Opposite: offer
what competitors do not clearly provide.

67
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:16,930
Third, the Law of Sacrifice:
focus on core subjects.

68
00:04:17,380 --> 00:04:20,299
Fourth, avoid the trap of line
extension by expanding the

69
00:04:20,350 --> 00:04:23,320
meaning of self-learning rather
than adding more products.

70
00:04:23,770 --> 00:04:27,354
Fifth, the Laws of the Mind and
Focus: communicate one clear word,

71
00:04:27,408 --> 00:04:31,100
"Design," starting with parents of
first- and second-grade students.

72
00:04:31,550 --> 00:04:34,388
Sixth, the Law of Candor:
acknowledge our smaller

73
00:04:34,446 --> 00:04:36,820
scale and focus on each child's learning.

74
00:04:38,570 --> 00:04:40,370
We have five core strategies.

75
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:44,000
First, redefine our category
as Learning Design.

76
00:04:44,450 --> 00:04:46,740
Second, focus on core subjects.

77
00:04:47,190 --> 00:04:50,980
Third, transform our locations
into Learning Design Studios.

78
00:04:51,430 --> 00:04:54,090
Fourth, combine AI with human coaching.

79
00:04:54,540 --> 00:04:57,730
And fifth, redefine
self-learning as an ability.

80
00:04:58,280 --> 00:05:02,450
These strategies work together to
build a stronger position for JEI.

81
00:05:04,200 --> 00:05:08,140
Our products should move beyond
question difficulty and volume.

82
00:05:08,590 --> 00:05:12,070
Instead, we will focus on
personalized learning roadmaps.

83
00:05:12,620 --> 00:05:14,450
The process has four steps.

84
00:05:14,900 --> 00:05:16,640
Assess each child's level.

85
00:05:17,090 --> 00:05:19,040
Set learning goals and a roadmap.

86
00:05:19,490 --> 00:05:21,780
Follow a personalized learning routine.

87
00:05:22,230 --> 00:05:25,400
And regularly review progress
and provide coaching.

88
00:05:25,950 --> 00:05:28,490
This cycle will guide
each child's learning.

89
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:33,460
JEI currently offers 17 subjects.

90
00:05:33,910 --> 00:05:37,150
We will focus our resources
on five priority subjects:

91
00:05:37,210 --> 00:05:40,150
Math, Korean, English,
Thinking Pizza, and Hanja.

92
00:05:40,600 --> 00:05:45,050
Other subjects may be reduced or managed
through partnerships and referrals.

93
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:48,384
Our initial target is parents
of first- and second-grade

94
00:05:48,434 --> 00:05:50,770
students choosing their
first learning program.

95
00:05:51,220 --> 00:05:54,860
By focusing our expertise, we can
build stronger customer trust.

96
00:05:56,610 --> 00:06:01,600
We plan to transform approximately 300
locations into Learning Design Studios.

97
00:06:02,050 --> 00:06:04,510
Each studio will provide three services.

98
00:06:04,960 --> 00:06:08,610
An AI Diagnostic Report to identify
the child's current level.

99
00:06:09,060 --> 00:06:12,460
A personalized three-month
and annual learning roadmap.

100
00:06:12,910 --> 00:06:16,890
And monthly coaching to review
progress and support learning habits.

101
00:06:17,440 --> 00:06:21,370
Our locations will become centers for
assessment, design, and coaching.

102
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:25,840
AI will provide personalized
questions, assess

103
00:06:25,899 --> 00:06:28,560
learning, grade answers,
and prepare reports.

104
00:06:29,010 --> 00:06:31,945
Learning Design Coaches will
use these results to create

105
00:06:31,997 --> 00:06:34,880
learning plans and support
motivation and study habits.

106
00:06:35,430 --> 00:06:39,230
AI handles learning data, while
teachers provide human guidance.

107
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:43,000
This combination is one
of JEI's key strengths.

108
00:06:43,650 --> 00:06:47,330
"AI provides the questions.
JEI designs the learning."

109
00:06:49,080 --> 00:06:53,160
JEI has promoted the Self-Learning
Method for nearly 50 years.

110
00:06:53,610 --> 00:06:57,680
But today, many education companies
use the term "self-learning."

111
00:06:58,130 --> 00:07:00,130
We need to give it a stronger meaning.

112
00:07:00,680 --> 00:07:03,270
Self-learning is not
simply studying alone.

113
00:07:03,720 --> 00:07:06,150
It is the ability to learn independently.

114
00:07:06,700 --> 00:07:11,320
JEI will focus on designing and
developing this ability in every child.

115
00:07:13,070 --> 00:07:16,440
"JEI designs children's ability
to learn on their own."

116
00:07:17,090 --> 00:07:19,530
This statement represents
our new direction.

117
00:07:19,980 --> 00:07:24,762
It creates a new category, establishes
"Design" as our key word, reflects the

118
00:07:24,824 --> 00:07:30,040
importance of human support in the AI era,
and builds on JEI's educational heritage.

119
00:07:30,490 --> 00:07:33,720
It will guide our products,
services, and communication.

120
00:07:35,470 --> 00:07:38,720
We will demonstrate Learning
Design through five services.

121
00:07:39,270 --> 00:07:41,130
An AI Diagnostic Report.

122
00:07:41,580 --> 00:07:43,570
A personalized learning roadmap.

123
00:07:44,020 --> 00:07:45,100
Monthly coaching.

124
00:07:45,550 --> 00:07:47,180
A learning routine record.

125
00:07:47,630 --> 00:07:50,210
And a Self-Learning Ability Growth Report.

126
00:07:50,760 --> 00:07:53,296
These services will help
parents see their children's

127
00:07:53,344 --> 00:07:55,450
progress and reduce
their management burden.

128
00:07:55,900 --> 00:07:59,960
To achieve this, we must first
strengthen our core-subject curricula.

129
00:08:01,710 --> 00:08:04,210
Our brand communication has three levels.

130
00:08:04,760 --> 00:08:08,290
First, key words: "Design"
and "Self-Learning Ability."

131
00:08:08,740 --> 00:08:12,580
Second, brand slogans, such as
"Learning Starts with Design."

132
00:08:13,030 --> 00:08:16,820
Third, campaign messages that
encourage parents to take action.

133
00:08:17,370 --> 00:08:19,740
We should not use too
many messages at once.

134
00:08:20,190 --> 00:08:24,530
One clear and consistent message
will help customers remember JEI.

135
00:08:26,280 --> 00:08:29,540
After 12 months, we will
evaluate five indicators.

136
00:08:30,090 --> 00:08:33,100
Brand association with
independent learning ability.

137
00:08:33,550 --> 00:08:36,370
The share of new first-
and second-grade students.

138
00:08:36,820 --> 00:08:40,250
A 100% delivery rate for
Learning Design Reports.

139
00:08:40,700 --> 00:08:43,320
Customer retention and cancellation rates.

140
00:08:43,770 --> 00:08:46,330
And the share of revenue
from core subjects.

141
00:08:46,880 --> 00:08:51,210
These indicators will show whether our
strategy is producing real results.

142
00:08:52,960 --> 00:08:57,690
Daekyo is known for levels, Kumon for
repetition, and Woongjin for its platform.

143
00:08:58,140 --> 00:09:01,940
JEI will focus on a new
opportunity: Learning Design.

144
00:09:02,490 --> 00:09:04,930
We want to become more
than a worksheet company.

145
00:09:05,380 --> 00:09:09,680
We want to become a company that designs
children's ability to learn independently.

146
00:09:10,330 --> 00:09:13,490
Our focus is clear: Designing
the Ability to Learn.

147
00:09:14,340 --> 00:09:14,950
Thank you.

